ce_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $971.9m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 133.6% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 7.2% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"},{"text":"Debt of $4.6bn against equity of $3.4bn. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526208992/0001193125-26-208992-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-208992"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 9.8% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (42,257 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526312814/0001193125-26-312814-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.2% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1973266/000119312526312814/0001193125-26-312814-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 11.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.11,"consecutive":2,"current":0.259,"current_display":"25.9%","threshold_display":"11.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 14.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.14,"consecutive":1,"current":0.072,"current_display":"7.2%","threshold_display":"14.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.90","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.9,"consecutive":1,"current":1.374,"current_display":"1.37","threshold_display":"1.90","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal 